<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1362–1440</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lord Grey of Ruthin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn, was an English marcher lord holding Ruthin in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. His land dispute with his neighbour <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a>, and Glyndŵr's failure to obtain justice, helped spark the Welsh revolt of 1400. Glyndŵr captured Grey in 1402 and released him only for a heavy ransom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reginald-grey-3rd-baron-grey-de-ruthyn.jpg" alt="Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A1 Aardvark · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Grey_of_Ruthin,_Denbighshire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
